Verse 1:
[F7]We [Bb]know not the hour of the [F]Master’s [F7]appear[Bb]ing;
Yet [F]signs all foretell that the [F7]moment is [Eb]near[Bb]ing
When He shall return ’tis the prom[F]ise [Bb7]most [Eb]cheering
But we [Bb]know [F7]not the [Bb]hour.
[F7]He will [Bb]come, let us watch and be ready;
[F7]He will [Bb]come, halle[F7]lujah! hallelujah!
He will [Bb]come in the clouds of His Fa[F]ther’s [Bb7]bright [Eb]glory—
But we [Bb]know [F7]not the [Bb]hour.

Refrain:
[F7]He [Bb]will come, [F]let us [F7]watch and [Bb]be ready;
